# Documentation
docs/
#
# One exception, and it is not documentation: the container entrypoint
# validates the mounted configuration against this file before staging it, so
# an image without it cannot start at all - `docker build` passes and
# `docker run` exits immediately.
#
# Re-included rather than copied elsewhere. The contract has fifteen references
# across the runtime, the tests, CI and the docs; a second copy beside the image
# would be a second source of truth that nothing keeps in step.
#
!docs/design/config.yml.example
README.md
LICENSE

# Docker
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Misc
*.md.bak

# Host frontend artifacts. The image builds its own dist in the node stage, so
# anything built on a developer's machine must not travel into the build
# context - it would be copied in and then shadowed, or worse, used.
frontend/app/node_modules/
frontend/app/dist/
frontend/app/coverage/
frontend/app/.vite/
